fix2.notes:
I checked each finding with a one-off probe over 40 generated 'torque' cases (seeds card:verify:0-39). Finding 1 holds: in 9 of the 40 cases the JR4 cannot reach 'selective-rca' anywhere on the search grid. Finding 3 also holds: in 36 of the 40 cases the smallest-excursion 'coaxial-rca' start leaves the class with a single torque step of 0.05.

Fix (findings 1 and 3), in /Users/qc25212/Downloads/Misc/Games and apps/Cath Simulator/src/mentor/skillCards.ts: the over-rotation card is now pinned to caseId 'easy-rca-0'. Preset 'torque', catheter JR4 and start class 'coaxial-rca' are unchanged, and so are the engagement thresholds and the shared findStartControls resolver. On easy-rca-0 the JR4 starts at insertion 0, torque 0. That is in the middle of the coaxial run, which spans torque -0.20 to 0.10. The catheter seats at torque 0.15 to 0.50 and drops back to coaxial at 0.55 and beyond, so over-rotating past the ostium can still happen and still be seen. I updated the comment on the template to match.

In /Users/qc25212/Downloads/Misc/Games and apps/Cath Simulator/src/mentor/mentor.test.ts I rewrote the over-rotation start test. It now asserts:
- the card is pinned to easy-rca-0;
- findStartControls(case, 'JR4', 'selective-rca') is not null;
- the start is right-sided, not selective, not in the conus, and nearer the RCA than the left main, at all three difficulties;
- a torque step of 0.05 either way stays 'coaxial-rca';
- the result is 'coaxial-rca' at every difficulty;
- a clockwise sweep reaches 'selective-rca' and then leaves it again.

Finding 2: /Users/qc25212/Downloads/Misc/Games and apps/Cath Simulator/src/ui/sections/Settings.tsx now has only the new intermediate line; the rejected part is explained above. I left src/ui/physics/types.test.ts alone because no finding concerned it.
